### Physics Engine

**Ship-Ball Physics (`SHIPCALC.CPP`):**
The crown jewel of the system - a sophisticated physics simulation for the ship-ball mechanics:

```cpp
// Thrust vector calculation
Vector thrustvectorcreate(int shipanglenr) {
    Vector Vthrustforce;
    float shipangle = ((float)shipanglenr / aantalangles) * P2I;
    
    Vthrustforce.X = thrustforce * -sin(shipangle);
    Vthrustforce.Y = thrustforce * cos(shipangle);
    
    return(Vthrustforce);
}

// Rotational acceleration from thrust
float rotateversnellingcalc(Vectors positions, Vector Vthrustforce) {
    float versnelling;
    float rotateforce;
    Vector factor;
    
    factor.X = (positions.ship.X - positions.ball.X) / stanglength; // sin
    factor.Y = (positions.ship.Y - positions.ball.Y) / stanglength; // cos
    
    rotateforce = Vthrustforce.X * factor.Y - Vthrustforce.Y * factor.X;
    versnelling = -rotateforce / (2* mass);
    
    return(versnelling);
}
```

**Physics Features:**
- Realistic momentum and inertia
- Gravity simulation with customizable strength
- Ship-ball tether mechanics with rotational physics
- Collision detection and response
- Hyperspace mechanics

### Game Loop Architecture

**Main Game Loop (`PLAYGAME.CPP`):**
```cpp
void Playgameman::startgame() {
    gamestatus playstatus;
    do {
        manageshipball();    // Update player physics
        managecore();        // Update world and rendering
        playstatus = user.updateuserdata();
    } while ((playstatus == busy) && (com.getescapestatus() != active));
    
    keuze = playstatus;
}
```

**Frame Management:**
- Consistent 13ms frame timing (≈77 FPS)
- Separate physics and rendering phases
- Entity management with cleanup cycles
- Input processing with command buffering

